1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,720
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,720 --> 00:00:04,960
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:06,120
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,120 --> 00:00:07,030
I had my right knee

5
00:00:07,030 --> 00:00:08,690
replaced two years ago.

6
00:00:08,690 --> 00:00:10,500
It has hurt every day
since.

7
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:11,840
Not surgery pain.

8
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:13,020
I know what that felt
like,

9
00:00:13,020 --> 00:00:13,870
and it went away.

10
00:00:13,870 --> 00:00:15,140
This is different.

11
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:15,950
Tight.

12
00:00:15,950 --> 00:00:16,850
Full.

13
00:00:16,850 --> 00:00:17,740
Like a band around

14
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:19,530
the joint that never
loosens.

15
00:00:19,530 --> 00:00:20,730
And for two years

16
00:00:20,730 --> 00:00:22,350
I've been told the same
thing.

17
00:00:22,350 --> 00:00:23,480
Give it time.

18
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:24,940
At six weeks it was
swelling,

19
00:00:24,940 --> 00:00:26,240
and swelling is normal.

20
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:27,240
At three months,

21
00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:28,390
give it six.

22
00:00:28,390 --> 00:00:29,100
At six months,

23
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:30,720
some knees take a full
year.

24
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:31,420
At a year,

25
00:00:31,420 --> 00:00:33,820
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

26
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:35,370
And I didn't just wait.

27
00:00:35,370 --> 00:00:36,940
We went down the list.

28
00:00:36,940 --> 00:00:38,330
More physical therapy.

29
00:00:38,330 --> 00:00:39,190
Every session,

30
00:00:39,190 --> 00:00:40,850
every exercise at home.

31
00:00:40,850 --> 00:00:42,010
I got stronger.

32
00:00:42,010 --> 00:00:43,710
The tightness never moved.

33
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:45,020
The pain pills helped,

34
00:00:45,020 --> 00:00:46,440
and that was the problem.

35
00:00:46,440 --> 00:00:48,380
I'm already on enough
every morning,

36
00:00:48,380 --> 00:00:49,360
and nobody could tell me

37
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:50,880
when I'd get to stop.

38
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:52,110
Then a nerve block.

39
00:00:52,110 --> 00:00:53,800
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

40
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:55,110
And after that, a second

41
00:00:55,110 --> 00:00:56,200
operation to go back

42
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:57,800
in and do it over.

43
00:00:57,800 --> 00:00:59,240
I said no.

44
00:00:59,240 --> 00:01:00,930
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

45
00:01:00,930 --> 00:01:02,110
and my knee felt like

46
00:01:02,110 --> 00:01:03,850
a band was wrapped around
it,

47
00:01:03,850 --> 00:01:06,470
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

48
00:01:06,470 --> 00:01:07,860
Every morning I took
something

49
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:08,880
for it and got

50
00:01:08,880 --> 00:01:10,110
on with my day.

51
00:01:10,110 --> 00:01:11,670
Couldn't do the stairs,

52
00:01:11,670 --> 00:01:12,750
couldn't stand at the
counter

53
00:01:12,750 --> 00:01:14,310
long enough to finish
dinner,

54
00:01:14,310 --> 00:01:15,840
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

55
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:18,200
game without shifting
every two minutes.

56
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:19,670
It woke me at night,

57
00:01:19,670 --> 00:01:22,050
and it turned ordinary
things,

58
00:01:22,050 --> 00:01:23,670
like getting in the car

59
00:01:23,670 --> 00:01:25,250
or up off the couch,

60
00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:26,380
into a decision.

61
00:01:26,380 --> 00:01:27,690
After a long and serious

62
00:01:27,690 --> 00:01:29,000
talk with my wife,

63
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,230
I went back in one more
time.

64
00:01:31,230 --> 00:01:32,380
That was the fourth set

65
00:01:32,380 --> 00:01:34,270
of X-rays on this knee.

66
00:01:34,270 --> 00:01:35,950
And like the three before
it,

67
00:01:35,950 --> 00:01:38,410
the answer was everything
looks great.

68
00:01:38,410 --> 00:01:40,130
No loosening, no
infection,

69
00:01:40,130 --> 00:01:41,150
nothing wrong.

70
00:01:41,150 --> 00:01:41,990
Only this time there

71
00:01:41,990 --> 00:01:43,390
was no new number.

72
00:01:43,390 --> 00:01:44,460
Nobody said

73
00:01:44,460 --> 00:01:45,730
give it another six
months.

74
00:01:45,730 --> 00:01:47,600
There was nothing left to
give it.

75
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:48,410
I sat in the parking

76
00:01:48,410 --> 00:01:49,660
lot for a while.

77
00:01:49,660 --> 00:01:51,170
Okay, I thought.

78
00:01:51,170 --> 00:01:52,760
Then explain this.

79
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:54,640
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

80
00:01:54,640 --> 00:01:56,140
I hit my breaking point.

81
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:58,210
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

82
00:01:58,210 --> 00:02:00,120
Everyone in the house was
asleep

83
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:01,750
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

84
00:02:01,750 --> 00:02:02,960
with my leg up,

85
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:04,460
trying to find any angle
where

86
00:02:04,460 --> 00:02:05,580
it didn't feel like
something

87
00:02:05,580 --> 00:02:07,030
was wrapped around my knee

88
00:02:07,030 --> 00:02:08,070
and tightening.

89
00:02:08,070 --> 00:02:10,400
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

90
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:12,610
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

91
00:02:12,610 --> 00:02:13,570
And I just thought,

92
00:02:13,570 --> 00:02:15,360
is this really my life
now?

93
00:02:15,360 --> 00:02:17,100
I can't live like this.

94
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:19,010
So I made myself a
promise.

95
00:02:19,010 --> 00:02:19,860
I wouldn't go a day

96
00:02:19,860 --> 00:02:21,660
without looking for an
answer.

97
00:02:21,660 --> 00:02:23,250
And when I found one,

98
00:02:23,250 --> 00:02:25,130
I'd share it with everyone

99
00:02:25,130 --> 00:02:27,020
going through the same
thing.

100
00:02:27,020 --> 00:02:28,130
So I got my laptop

101
00:02:28,130 --> 00:02:30,040
out and went looking.

102
00:02:30,040 --> 00:02:31,400
Not for a product.

103
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:32,910
For an explanation.

104
00:02:32,910 --> 00:02:34,590
Mayo Clinic forums,

105
00:02:34,590 --> 00:02:36,700
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

106
00:02:36,700 --> 00:02:39,360
doctor videos, medical
animations.

107
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:40,290
And that's when I found

108
00:02:40,290 --> 00:02:42,090
a video from a physical
therapist

109
00:02:42,090 --> 00:02:42,620
named Dr.

110
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:44,630
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

111
00:02:44,630 --> 00:02:46,670
had been through exactly
this.

112
00:02:46,670 --> 00:02:48,850
But before I say anything
else,

113
00:02:48,850 --> 00:02:50,650
I want to be straight with
you.

114
00:02:50,650 --> 00:02:53,050
You've already had
something work fast.

115
00:02:53,050 --> 00:02:53,990
The ice.

116
00:02:53,990 --> 00:02:55,620
The first week of a new
pill.

117
00:02:55,620 --> 00:02:57,540
The good day after a
session.

118
00:02:57,540 --> 00:02:58,630
Then it wore off.

119
00:02:58,630 --> 00:03:01,230
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

120
00:03:01,230 --> 00:03:03,340
Fast relief isn't relief.

121
00:03:03,340 --> 00:03:04,650
It's a preview.

122
00:03:04,650 --> 00:03:05,670
So I'm not going to tell

123
00:03:05,670 --> 00:03:07,120
you this works fast.

124
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:08,330
It doesn't.

125
00:03:08,330 --> 00:03:10,160
But if you're willing to
be patient,

126
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:10,890
and to look at what's

127
00:03:10,890 --> 00:03:12,180
going on around your new
knee

128
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:13,780
instead of inside it,
there

129
00:03:13,780 --> 00:03:15,990
is a real reason it still
hurts.

130
00:03:15,990 --> 00:03:18,310
And something you can do
about it.

131
00:03:18,310 --> 00:03:19,610
Let me explain what he
said,

132
00:03:19,610 --> 00:03:21,040
because this is what
changed

133
00:03:21,040 --> 00:03:22,490
everything for me.

134
00:03:22,490 --> 00:03:24,580
He started with the
basics.

135
00:03:24,580 --> 00:03:26,080
A knee replacement takes
out

136
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:27,820
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

137
00:03:27,820 --> 00:03:29,230
in metal and plastic.

138
00:03:29,230 --> 00:03:31,250
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

139
00:03:31,250 --> 00:03:33,070
you had before the
operation.

140
00:03:33,070 --> 00:03:34,730
That part I already knew.

141
00:03:34,730 --> 00:03:36,070
But then he explained
something

142
00:03:36,070 --> 00:03:37,440
nobody had ever told me.

143
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:38,260
He said,

144
00:03:38,260 --> 00:03:39,950
think about a swollen foot

145
00:03:39,950 --> 00:03:41,640
inside a shoe.

146
00:03:41,640 --> 00:03:43,040
The shoe didn't shrink.

147
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:45,250
Your foot is taking up
more room,

148
00:03:45,250 --> 00:03:46,690
so everything feels
cramped

149
00:03:46,690 --> 00:03:48,290
and tight and squeezed.

150
00:03:48,290 --> 00:03:49,180
Your new knee sits

151
00:03:49,180 --> 00:03:50,690
in a limited space with
living

152
00:03:50,690 --> 00:03:52,730
tissue packed all around
it.

153
00:03:52,730 --> 00:03:54,590
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

154
00:03:54,590 --> 00:03:56,420
had to work through that
tissue.

155
00:03:56,420 --> 00:03:59,300
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

156
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:00,830
At first that's normal.

157
00:04:00,830 --> 00:04:02,450
But in some people that
swelling can

158
00:04:02,450 --> 00:04:05,230
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

159
00:04:05,230 --> 00:04:07,090
And swollen tissue takes
up more

160
00:04:07,090 --> 00:04:09,050
room than calm tissue
does.

161
00:04:09,050 --> 00:04:10,410
So when you bend,

162
00:04:10,410 --> 00:04:12,330
that tissue gets
compressed.

163
00:04:12,330 --> 00:04:13,500
When you straighten,

164
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:15,070
it gets pulled tight.

165
00:04:15,070 --> 00:04:16,270
That's the band.

166
00:04:16,270 --> 00:04:18,660
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

167
00:04:18,660 --> 00:04:19,650
And you start being

168
00:04:19,650 --> 00:04:20,780
the one who says,

169
00:04:20,780 --> 00:04:21,640
you go ahead.

170
00:04:21,640 --> 00:04:23,010
I'll stay here.

171
00:04:23,010 --> 00:04:24,840
And that's exactly why so
much

172
00:04:24,840 --> 00:04:27,230
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

173
00:04:27,230 --> 00:04:29,380
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

174
00:04:29,380 --> 00:04:30,430
around the knee.

175
00:04:30,430 --> 00:04:31,430
Worth doing,

176
00:04:31,430 --> 00:04:32,420
and I'd done it.

177
00:04:32,420 --> 00:04:33,790
It does nothing about
tissue

178
00:04:33,790 --> 00:04:35,080
taking up room.

179
00:04:35,080 --> 00:04:36,570
A nerve block quiets

180
00:04:36,570 --> 00:04:39,080
the nerve carrying the
signal.

181
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:41,160
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

182
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:42,780
But when that irritated
tissue

183
00:04:42,780 --> 00:04:44,390
finally calms down,

184
00:04:44,390 --> 00:04:45,850
it holds less fluid,

185
00:04:45,850 --> 00:04:47,500
and it takes up less room.

186
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:48,850
Less room taken up means

187
00:04:48,850 --> 00:04:51,000
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

188
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,160
That's what takes the
pressure off.

189
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:54,650
After two years of this,

190
00:04:54,650 --> 00:04:56,590
it finally made sense.

191
00:04:56,590 --> 00:04:58,800
The problem was never the
new knee.

192
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:00,810
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

193
00:05:00,810 --> 00:05:02,480
He calls it the squeeze.

194
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:05,070
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

195
00:05:05,070 --> 00:05:06,140
I'd bought knee sleeves,

196
00:05:06,140 --> 00:05:07,920
compression braces,
creams,

197
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:09,450
half of Amazon really,

198
00:05:09,450 --> 00:05:11,240
and all any of it gave me

199
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:12,180
was an hour.

200
00:05:12,180 --> 00:05:13,090
I even looked at going

201
00:05:13,090 --> 00:05:15,140
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

202
00:05:15,140 --> 00:05:16,930
But at $200 a session

203
00:05:16,930 --> 00:05:19,170
with nothing covered by
insurance,

204
00:05:19,170 --> 00:05:20,850
that was a quick no.

205
00:05:20,850 --> 00:05:21,930
Then one night I went

206
00:05:21,930 --> 00:05:23,300
back to that knee
replacement

207
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:25,260
group and actually read
it.

208
00:05:25,260 --> 00:05:26,600
Thousands of people,

209
00:05:26,600 --> 00:05:28,380
years out from surgery,

210
00:05:28,380 --> 00:05:30,970
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

211
00:05:30,970 --> 00:05:32,670
nobody could explain.

212
00:05:32,670 --> 00:05:34,350
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

213
00:05:34,350 --> 00:05:36,570
the same thing kept coming
up.

214
00:05:36,570 --> 00:05:38,020
This one device,

215
00:05:38,020 --> 00:05:40,480
and people saying it was
the first

216
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:41,880
thing that made a
difference.

217
00:05:41,880 --> 00:05:43,890
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

218
00:05:43,890 --> 00:05:45,240
alright, here it comes,

219
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:46,700
he's selling me something,

220
00:05:46,700 --> 00:05:48,610
let me shut that down
right now.

221
00:05:48,610 --> 00:05:50,480
I'm only here because I
made myself

222
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:52,850
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

223
00:05:52,850 --> 00:05:53,890
that if I ever found

224
00:05:53,890 --> 00:05:55,280
something that helped,

225
00:05:55,280 --> 00:05:56,630
I'd say so.

226
00:05:56,630 --> 00:05:58,320
It's called the KenRelief
Red

227
00:05:58,320 --> 00:05:59,980
Light Therapy Wrap.

228
00:05:59,980 --> 00:06:02,470
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

229
00:06:02,470 --> 00:06:03,800
It looked like the cheap

230
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:06,420
knee sleeves off Amazon

231
00:06:06,420 --> 00:06:08,320
that did nothing for me.

232
00:06:08,320 --> 00:06:10,610
But I went to their
website anyway,

233
00:06:10,610 --> 00:06:11,770
just to see what all

234
00:06:11,770 --> 00:06:13,360
the fuss was about.

235
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:15,190
It's the same red light
therapy

236
00:06:15,190 --> 00:06:18,240
clinics charge $200 a
session

237
00:06:18,240 --> 00:06:20,470
for, off machines that
cost

238
00:06:20,470 --> 00:06:22,240
fifty thousand dollars,

239
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:23,580
in a wrap you plug

240
00:06:23,580 --> 00:06:25,390
into the wall at home.

241
00:06:25,390 --> 00:06:27,400
Two hundred and forty
lights.

242
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:29,730
Red at 660 nanometers

243
00:06:29,730 --> 00:06:32,290
and near-infrared at 850,

244
00:06:32,290 --> 00:06:34,860
run together for the
strongest effect.

245
00:06:34,860 --> 00:06:36,670
Four strength levels.

246
00:06:36,670 --> 00:06:38,940
A five to thirty minute
timer.

247
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:40,770
Then I saw the guarantee.

248
00:06:40,770 --> 00:06:42,290
Ninety days.

249
00:06:42,290 --> 00:06:44,000
Results or your money
back,

250
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,320
no questions, no store
credit,

251
00:06:46,320 --> 00:06:48,440
and you don't even send it
back.

252
00:06:48,440 --> 00:06:50,800
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

253
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:52,760
days to change my mind.

254
00:06:52,760 --> 00:06:53,930
There wasn't much to lose,

255
00:06:53,930 --> 00:06:54,950
so I ordered it.

256
00:06:54,950 --> 00:06:56,390
Two of them, actually.

257
00:06:56,390 --> 00:06:58,630
Only the right knee was
replaced,

258
00:06:58,630 --> 00:07:00,690
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

259
00:07:00,690 --> 00:07:03,160
and I'd done it for two
years.

260
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:05,230
The left one was carrying
the difference.

261
00:07:05,230 --> 00:07:05,810
When it came,

262
00:07:05,810 --> 00:07:07,990
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

263
00:07:07,990 --> 00:07:09,190
because I'd been let down
too

264
00:07:09,190 --> 00:07:11,070
many times to get excited.

265
00:07:11,070 --> 00:07:12,670
What I felt was warmth.

266
00:07:12,670 --> 00:07:14,720
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

267
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:16,540
More like it was coming
from inside

268
00:07:16,540 --> 00:07:18,980
the knee and spreading
around it.

269
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:20,040
And that was it.

270
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:21,730
That was the whole
experience.

271
00:07:21,730 --> 00:07:22,960
When I took it off,

272
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:23,850
I'll be honest,

273
00:07:23,850 --> 00:07:25,770
nothing dramatic had
happened.

274
00:07:25,770 --> 00:07:27,410
And after what that video
said,

275
00:07:27,410 --> 00:07:29,580
that's exactly what I
expected.

276
00:07:29,580 --> 00:07:30,310
What was different

277
00:07:30,310 --> 00:07:31,280
was that for the first

278
00:07:31,280 --> 00:07:32,380
time in two years

279
00:07:32,380 --> 00:07:33,720
I'd done something for my
knee

280
00:07:33,720 --> 00:07:35,210
instead of to it.

281
00:07:35,210 --> 00:07:36,250
Twenty minutes,

282
00:07:36,250 --> 00:07:37,450
in my own chair.

283
00:07:37,450 --> 00:07:39,480
No drive, no copay.

284
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:41,730
They say twenty minutes.

285
00:07:41,730 --> 00:07:42,820
I did thirty,

286
00:07:42,820 --> 00:07:44,090
twice a day,

287
00:07:44,090 --> 00:07:46,290
lowest setting that first
week.

288
00:07:46,290 --> 00:07:47,780
I put it on the calendar.

289
00:07:47,780 --> 00:07:48,490
The first week,

290
00:07:48,490 --> 00:07:49,340
I couldn't have told

291
00:07:49,340 --> 00:07:51,180
you if anything was
happening.

292
00:07:51,180 --> 00:07:52,050
I tried not to get

293
00:07:52,050 --> 00:07:52,750
my hopes up.

294
00:07:52,750 --> 00:07:54,140
I'd had things help for a
week

295
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:55,240
and then stop.

296
00:07:55,240 --> 00:07:56,490
But somewhere in the
second week

297
00:07:56,490 --> 00:07:57,570
I noticed I'd come down

298
00:07:57,570 --> 00:07:59,490
the stairs without holding
the rail.

299
00:07:59,490 --> 00:08:00,980
I hadn't decided to.

300
00:08:00,980 --> 00:08:01,980
I just did it,

301
00:08:01,980 --> 00:08:03,640
then stopped halfway down

302
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:05,120
because I realized.

303
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:06,720
By the end of the fourth
week

304
00:08:06,720 --> 00:08:07,820
I'd slept through the
night

305
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:09,300
four times running.

306
00:08:09,300 --> 00:08:10,640
I stood at the counter

307
00:08:10,640 --> 00:08:11,890
and finished making dinner

308
00:08:11,890 --> 00:08:13,830
without looking for the
stool.

309
00:08:13,830 --> 00:08:15,470
None of that is dramatic.

310
00:08:15,470 --> 00:08:16,440
All of it was gone

311
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:17,770
for two years.

312
00:08:17,770 --> 00:08:19,400
A few weeks later my wife
asked

313
00:08:19,400 --> 00:08:20,350
if I wanted to walk

314
00:08:20,350 --> 00:08:22,510
the long way around the
block.

315
00:08:22,510 --> 00:08:23,600
And for the first time

316
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:24,400
in two years,

317
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:25,730
I said yes.

318
00:08:25,730 --> 00:08:27,600
I wanted to understand
why,

319
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:29,280
so I read the whole thing.

320
00:08:29,280 --> 00:08:31,010
It comes down to four
steps.

321
00:08:31,010 --> 00:08:31,980
One.

322
00:08:31,980 --> 00:08:33,730
The tissue around a new
knee can

323
00:08:33,730 --> 00:08:37,000
stay inflamed long after
surgery is over.

324
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:37,920
Two.

325
00:08:37,920 --> 00:08:40,460
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

326
00:08:40,460 --> 00:08:41,500
so it takes up more

327
00:08:41,500 --> 00:08:42,970
room than it should.

328
00:08:42,970 --> 00:08:43,910
Three.

329
00:08:43,910 --> 00:08:45,590
There's only so much room
in there.

330
00:08:45,590 --> 00:08:47,430
Bending compresses it.

331
00:08:47,430 --> 00:08:49,120
Straightening pulls it
tight.

332
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:50,680
That's the squeeze.

333
00:08:50,680 --> 00:08:51,720
Four.

334
00:08:51,720 --> 00:08:54,040
Red and near-infrared
light have been

335
00:08:54,040 --> 00:08:56,260
studied for calming that
inflammation,

336
00:08:56,260 --> 00:08:57,600
so the swelling and the
pressure

337
00:08:57,600 --> 00:08:59,050
can come down with it.

338
00:08:59,050 --> 00:09:00,050
In a randomized trial,

339
00:09:00,050 --> 00:09:01,620
patients given light
therapy after

340
00:09:01,620 --> 00:09:02,400
a knee replacement

341
00:09:02,400 --> 00:09:03,150
had less pain,

342
00:09:03,150 --> 00:09:04,110
less swelling

343
00:09:04,110 --> 00:09:05,700
and better early movement
than

344
00:09:05,700 --> 00:09:06,970
those who weren't.

345
00:09:06,970 --> 00:09:09,430
A 2025 review said the
same,

346
00:09:09,430 --> 00:09:10,590
and was clear the evidence

347
00:09:10,590 --> 00:09:11,770
is still limited.

348
00:09:11,770 --> 00:09:13,320
I probably sound like a
broken

349
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:14,900
record to my family.

350
00:09:14,900 --> 00:09:16,840
But after two years of
doing everything

351
00:09:16,840 --> 00:09:18,710
I was told and getting
nowhere,

352
00:09:18,710 --> 00:09:20,040
you have no idea what it's

353
00:09:20,040 --> 00:09:21,640
like to sleep through the
night,

354
00:09:21,640 --> 00:09:22,900
say yes to the walk,

355
00:09:22,900 --> 00:09:24,600
and get my life back.

356
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:25,970
So take it from me.

357
00:09:25,970 --> 00:09:27,310
Don't spend another year
waiting

358
00:09:27,310 --> 00:09:28,500
